{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Blink doorbell feels like a useful next purchase because door alerts and two-way audio add a security function alongside my Echo devices.",
    "Charging cables and removable storage fit my history of buying practical accessories, while Echo Auto suggests a possible new use for Alexa beyond the devices I already own."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "An older Echo Dot feels redundant after my fourth-generation Dot purchase, and a larger Echo Show is less compelling when I recently bought a Show 5 and its stand.",
    "Desktop memory and an internal SSD require an upgrade plan and compatible hardware that my accessory purchases do not establish. The headphone adapter also solves a connection problem I have not expressed."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repeated Echo purchases seem to be taken as a reason to suggest more Echo devices, even when they repeat a function I recently covered.",
    "My interest in computer accessories and external storage seems to be stretched into an interest in specialized internal computer upgrades."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases matter: the Show 5 stand suggests I am equipping the display I already have, rather than looking for another screen.",
    "A useful accessory still needs a specific purpose and compatible device. I would check those before buying a cable or memory card, and I would try the doorbell before adding a separate camera."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions recognize my interest in practical electronics and Alexa, but miss the difference between adding a useful function and duplicating something I recently bought."
}"}
